--- !-- Discrete Hodge theorem (operator form).  `(→)`: `Δ x = 0` makes the sum of the two
---    nonnegative energies vanish, so each vanishes; `inner_self_eq_zero` gives `d x = 0`,
---    `e* x = 0`.  `(←)`: both vanish so `Δ x = d* 0 + e 0 = 0`. -- !--
